# Rust
/target
# defensive: a *relative* CARGO_TARGET_DIR (e.g. an IDE env misconfig) creates
# per-crate nested target dirs — never let them pollute the tree
**/target/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# Cargo.lock IS committed: this workspace ships a server binary (not a library),
# so a pinned lockfile gives reproducible `--locked` container builds.

# Env / secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
# The committed CNF SMART-lane TEST key is the one deliberate exception —
# a static test-only issuer key (docs/conformance/party/smart/README.md),
# never production material.
!docs/conformance/party/smart/cnf-smart-test.key.pem
*.key

# Editor / OS
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.DS_Store

# Claude Code local overrides
CLAUDE.local.md
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/.session-start-head
.claude/.session-start-time

# Coverage / bench artifacts
/coverage
lcov.info
*.profraw

# sccache
.sccache/

.claude/worktrees

# Docs website build artifacts (assembled by scripts/site/build.sh; never committed)
/_site
/website/book/book
/docs-dist
/.latest-src
_check/

# Stray local build artifacts
*.rlib
website/book/generated/
__pycache__/
docs/conformance/*/perf-corpus-*.json
# The HAR recording of a conformance run holds the server's response bodies
# verbatim; it stays where the run is kept and is never committed.
docs/conformance/*/recording.har
# The JUnit and CTRF views of a run are CI views, kept as run artifacts; the
# record commits results.json and summary.md only.
docs/conformance/*/junit.xml
docs/conformance/*/ctrf.json
# A development-profile run is published beside the record, never committed
# into it (scripts/conformance.sh, CONF_PROFILE=development).
docs/conformance/ferroehr-development/

# The viewer keeps NO local store: query grouping is derived from the
# namespace in each stored query's qualified name, and the directory create
# flow commits an empty root, so nothing is written beside the binary any more.
# These names are the belt against an OLDER viewer binary run inside the
# checkout ever re-appearing as tracked files.
/viewer-groups.json
/viewer-folder-templates.json
/viewer-*.json.tmp

# insta pending snapshots — never committed (see the snapshot-root issue)
**/*.snap.new

# cargo-cyclonedx output. SBOMs are generated per release and attached to it
# as an attested asset, never committed — a checked-in SBOM describes whatever
# graph happened to be resolved the day someone ran it.
*.cdx.json

# SNOMED CT release packages, dropped in the repository root so the terminology
# probe can find them (scripts/deploy-probes/terminology.sh).
#
# These are LICENSED content under a SNOMED International Affiliate agreement —
# they may not be committed, published, or redistributed. This entry is the
# guard: the archives are ~1 GB and would otherwise be one `git add -A` away
# from the history, where removing them means rewriting it.
SnomedCT_*.zip
doc_SnomedCT*.pdf

# The default targets of the opt-in `backup` compose profile
# (`docker compose --profile backup run --rm ferroehr-backup-clinical`).
# A dump of a real deployment carries clinical data, from the second directory
# the identities of its subjects, and from the third the map between them —
# none belongs in a git history, and the three are separate directories for
# exactly that reason.
/backups/

# The Helm chart dependencies, fetched by `helm dependency build` from
# deploy/helm/ferroehr/Chart.lock.
deploy/helm/ferroehr/charts/
